    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but it's not about me finding a \"new path.\" that's just more noise, more failure. if a tree is rotten, you don't try to teach the rot to be a better branch, you just cut it out so the rest of the tree can live. i just want to be a solution for once instead of the problem. i want to know if there's any version of this where my absence actually does them a favor.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
